  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose, $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma$ are the roots of the equation $\\mathrm{x}^3+\\mathrm{qx}+\\mathrm{r}=0($ with $\\mathrm{r} \\neq 0)$ and they are in A.P. Then the rank of the matrix $\\left(\\begin{array}{lll}\\alpha & \\beta & \\gamma \\\\ \\beta & \\gamma & \\alpha \\\\ \\gamma & \\alpha & \\beta\\end{array}\\right)$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$3$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of the above",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, $\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=0$\n$\\left|\\begin{array}{lll}\n\\alpha & \\beta & \\gamma \\\\\n\\beta & \\gamma & \\alpha \\\\\n\\gamma & \\alpha & \\beta\n\\end{array}\\right|=-\\left(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3-3 \\alpha \\beta \\gamma\\right)=0(\\because \\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=0)$\n\nGiven, $2 \\beta=\\alpha+\\gamma \\Rightarrow 3 \\beta=\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma \\Rightarrow \\beta=0 \\Rightarrow r=0$ (But given $r \\neq 0$ )"
  }
}